    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Indian nationalism evolved due to Western education, economic exploitation, growth of press, racial discrimination (Ilbert Bill controversy), and modern transport &amp; communication. The Revolt of 1857 marked the beginning of organized resistance.",
      "id": "ru397c1"
    },
